# Nares 1-km regional run (2026-10-07). Adapted from pan_AO input/data.cal.
# Comments below that are not marked 'Nares' are inherited from pan_AO
# (dates, job ids and file names in them refer to pan_AO).
#
#
# *******************
# Calendar Parameters
# *******************
# startDate_1 LOCKED 2026-10-02 to the actual regional-run start date.
# Was 19920101 -- the parent LLC270 v5r1 calendar BASE, correct as a
# placeholder but wrong as a start date once the ICs were pinned to parent
# iteration 736344. That iteration is 1992-01-01 + 736344*1200 s =
# 883,612,800 s = 10227.0 days exactly = 2020-01-01 00:00:00 (28 yr, 7 leap
# days -- verified by calendar arithmetic, not assumed).
#
# This value must agree with the obcs{N,S,E,W}startdate1 = 20200101 already
# wired in data.exf (2026-10-01) and with kerguelen, which runs 20200101 off
# the SAME parent pickups at the same iteration. Leaving 19920101 here would
# have offset the model clock 28 years from its own boundary forcing: EXF
# would have read OBCS/ERA5 records from the wrong end of the archive, and
# because every file involved exists and is the right size, it would have
# run without error.
 &CAL_NML
 TheCalendar='gregorian',
 startDate_1=20150101,
 startDate_2=000000,
 calendarDumps = .TRUE.,
 &
